<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    Every list of planet layers that names vanilla's Surface also names the ring's def, so what's allowed or barred on a
    planet's surface is allowed or barred on the ring the same way. Without it, on a ring: raids and visitors never drop
    in by pod (the pod arrival modes and the Empire's and other factions' arrival whitelists), sieges and Anomaly's
    psychic rituals never happen, mortars can't be manned, the give-up-and-leave mental break never fires, and Odyssey's
    site quests that whitelist Surface never find a site. The lists are named layerWhitelist, layerBlacklist,
    arrivalLayerWhitelist, planetLayerWhitelist, layerDefs and so on, in defs and in quest scripts alike; every element
    whose name has "Layer" or starts with "layer" counts. Planet worlds have no ring layer, so the extra entry changes
    nothing there. Lists other mods add after this patch, or from code, aren't covered.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>Defs//*[(contains(name(), 'Layer') or starts-with(name(), 'layer')) and li = 'Surface' and not(li = 'RW_Ring')]</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RW_Ring</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
